      "title": "Identifying Parallel Vectors From a Diagram"
    },
    "question": {
      ":question/id": "30f8b606-339b-5be3-b437-cf7c9bea7d53",
      ":question/problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/generate/scratch/17592186096700/plots/05ebbede528988545559804360556ad7f243275b30dcf79f336814b09fed2ce2.png)\n\nConsider the diagram that is shown above. Which of the following statements are true?\n\n1. $b =-e$\n2. $c =-d$\n3. $b = e$",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "fda44c1f-7fca-5311-b908-f541d82fda54",
          ":answer-field/key": "selection",
          ":answer-field/type": ":answer-field.type/radio",
          ":answer-field/choices": [
            {
              ":answer/id": "00537e38-de54-5b88-97c1-b4d218008201",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/text",
              ":answer/value": "I only"
            },
            {
              ":answer/id": "88ec636b-bf16-537d-bf8f-5dcc18eecb96",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/text",
              ":answer/value": "I and II only"
            },
            {
              ":answer/id": "9e4b2c3c-d0ff-5657-8629-67b1509a6703",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/text",
              ":answer/value": "II and III only"
            },
            {
              ":answer/id": "c67839f4-815f-5a4d-85ea-5fb75adee464",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/text",
              ":answer/value": "I and III only"
            },
            {
              ":answer/id": "386d13b3-10af-50f2-9903-3f65af97610d",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/text",
              ":answer/value": "III only"
            }
          ],
          ":answer-field/correct": [
            ":answer/id",
            "386d13b3-10af-50f2-9903-3f65af97610d"
          ]
        }
      ],
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/worked-solution": "- Statement I is false. The vectors $b$ and $e$ have the same direction. So, $b\\neq-e$.\n- Statement II is false. The vectors $c$ and $d$ have the same direction. So, $c\\neq-d$.\n- Statement III is true. Indeed, vectors $e$ and $b$ are parallel and have the same direction. Also, the magnitude of $b$ is $1$ times the magnitude of $e$. So, $b=e$.\n\nTherefore, only statement III is true."
    },
