      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
      ":question/worked-solution": "- Statement I is true. Indeed, vectors $e$ and $b$ are parallel and have opposite directions. Also, the magnitude of $b$ is $2$ times the magnitude of $e$. So, $b=-2e$.\n- Statement II is false. The vectors $c$ and $d$ have the same direction. So, $c\\neq-d$.\n- Statement III is false. The vectors $b$ and $e$ have opposite directions. So, $b\\neq2e$.\n\nTherefore, only statement I is true."
