  {
    "knowledge_point": {
      "db_id": 17592186096700,
      "id": "dc5bab6c-1ce7-58b5-a59d-cff2ce35ecca",
      "title": "Identifying Parallel Vectors From a Diagram"
    },
    "question": {
      ":question/id": "d831b7f5-8db2-5fa8-ab4e-3b4e0be11e9a",
      ":question/problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/generate/scratch/17592186096700/plots/9ad8b5ad3f97f0b0f946ccf7608b0b4b9e528903cd9b800ccf9654e401ec2bad.png)\n\nConsider the diagram that is shown above. Which of the following statements are true?\n\n1. $b =-\\frac{3}{2}e$\n2. $c =-d$\n3. $b = \\frac{3}{2}e$",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "f470dc70-df66-59b9-9f18-5beff4ce18b9",
          ":answer-field/key": "selection",
          ":answer-field/type": ":answer-field.type/radio",
          ":answer-field/choices": [
            {
              ":answer/id": "ed5d57e3-4b0e-5578-9e27-f550a12f4d95",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/text",
              ":answer/value": "I and III only"
            },
            {
              ":answer/id": "f5fba7d7-372a-5fd9-8be2-d1d74e660e9d",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/text",
              ":answer/value": "I only"
            },
            {
              ":answer/id": "a7a5ebe1-80f7-52b8-9722-b062d4ea813c",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/text",
              ":answer/value": "II and III only"
            },
            {
              ":answer/id": "62377f50-34ce-5572-8c9f-4245e57621d3",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/text",
              ":answer/value": "III only"
            },
            {
              ":answer/id": "98962759-febd-5e50-8f04-c4d95580714b",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/text",
              ":answer/value": "I and II only"
            }
          ],
          ":answer-field/correct": [
            ":answer/id",
            "62377f50-34ce-5572-8c9f-4245e57621d3"
          ]
        }
      ],
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/hard",
      ":question/worked-solution": "- Statement I is false. The vectors $b$ and $e$ have the same direction. So, $b\\neq-\\frac{3}{2}e$.\n- Statement II is false. The vectors $c$ and $d$ have the same direction. So, $c\\neq-d$.\n- Statement III is true. Indeed, vectors $e$ and $b$ are parallel and have the same direction. Also, the magnitude of $b$ is $\\frac{3}{2}$ times the magnitude of $e$. So, $b=\\frac{3}{2}e$.\n\nTherefore, only statement III is true."
    },
